  "answers": [
    "I can't tell whether your heart rate stayed elevated all day on October 2, 2026. The local data doesn't cover the whole day.\n\n- **What's stored for that date:** three heart rate readings, all from 10:00 to 10:02 AM local time: 100, 101, and 102 bpm. The provider's records say these come from exercise windows only.\n- **What's missing:** there are no readings for the rest of the day, so I can't say whether your heart rate was elevated at other times. Missing readings aren't the same as a low or normal heart rate.\n\nThe three readings show that your heart rate was around 100 bpm during a 10 AM window, which may have been a workout or activity. That's a single short window, not an all-day pattern.\n\nTo check the full day, I can import whole-day heart rate from Google. That's a larger download, about 37 MB per day, and I'd need to start it as a background job. Let me know if you want that."
  ],
